* A file-reading operation fails with ENOENT in production but works locally. How would you troubleshoot it?
* Your application receives EACCES when writing a file on a Linux server. What would you investigate?
* Two requests update the same JSON file simultaneously, and some data is lost. How would you prevent this?
* A server crashes after processing thousands of files because of exhausted file descriptors. How would you diagnose and resolve it?
* Your application needs to process a directory containing millions of files. How would you design the processing workflow?
* A file upload API allows users to specify filenames containing ../ sequences. How would you secure it?
* A file watcher misses changes during periods of heavy activity. How would you make the processing reliable?
* Your application processes the same file multiple times because of duplicate watcher events. How would you prevent duplicate processing?
* A file is read while another process is writing to it, resulting in incomplete data. How would you handle this?
* A large file copy operation consumes too much memory. How would you redesign it using streams?
* A stream pipeline stops unexpectedly when the destination disk becomes full. How would you handle the failure?
* Your application must process incoming files in order, but multiple files arrive simultaneously. How would you guarantee ordering?
* Several workers attempt to process the same file at the same time. How would you coordinate them?
* Your application writes a configuration file, but a crash leaves it partially updated. How would you prevent this?
* A file-processing service needs to resume after a server restart without reprocessing completed files. How would you design it?
* Your application needs to verify that downloaded files are not corrupted. How would you implement integrity checks?
* A temporary-file directory grows continuously and fills the disk. How would you implement cleanup safely?
* File paths behave differently between Windows development machines and Linux production servers. How would you resolve the problem?
* A symbolic link points outside the intended storage directory. How would you prevent unauthorized file access?
* Your service processes files from multiple directories, but one directory contains malformed files. How would you isolate failures?
* A file-processing task blocks other requests because it performs CPU-intensive parsing. How would you improve responsiveness?
* The libuv thread pool becomes saturated due to heavy file-system activity. How would you identify and mitigate the bottleneck?
* A deployment changes directory permissions and breaks file writes. How would you make deployment and permission management reliable?
